From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: axp20x-pek: a press stops a suspend

The power key's interrupt only reports the key. A press while the system
suspends, before suspend_device_irqs(), is handled as usual: it wakes
nothing, and its events wait in the input queue for the next wakeup. On
the PinePhone, pressed again within the half second s2idle takes to get
there, the phone stayed asleep (to the user: frozen), and once a later
press woke it, the queued presses reached phone-ui as new ones and put it
back to sleep 0.2 s after waking.

Report a wakeup event, as gpio-keys does: the suspend stops, or s2idle
wakes up right away.

---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c
@@ -211,6 +211,14 @@
 
 	input_sync(idev);
 
+	/*
+	 * A press while the system suspends: stop it, as gpio-keys does. Before
+	 * suspend_device_irqs() the interrupt is handled as usual and would wake
+	 * nothing, the press only reaching user space with the next wakeup.
+	 */
+	if (device_may_wakeup(idev->dev.parent))
+		pm_wakeup_event(idev->dev.parent, 0);
+
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
